 *   **Time Complexity:** Depends on the number of null collisions [S4]. In dense regions, it approaches the cost of homogeneous sampling [G]. In sparse regions, it degrades linearly with the ratio $\sigma_t^{\max} / \sigma_t(\mathbf{x})$ [S4].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the volume data and the majorant value [S2, S4]. No additional subdivision structures are strictly required, though hierarchical majorants may add overhead [S4].
-*   **Measured Performance:** Rendering a cloud with delta tracking and Next Event Estimation (10 samples per pixel) took 248 seconds on the tested hardware [S2].
+*   **Measured Performance:** Rendering a cloud with delta tracking and Next Event Estimation (10 samples per pixel) took 248 seconds on the tested hardware [S2, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths:** Unbiased; handles arbitrary heterogeneous media without subdivision; simple implementation [S2, S4].
 *   **Limitations:** High variance in sparse volumes; inefficient for large empty spaces; requires global majorant computation [S2, S4].
